# Rust maintenance submission — ABI v2

Upgraded the predecessor in place to ABI v2 and deterministic high/normal
scheduling. Schema 1 and v1 datadirs are preserved. The delivered Linux AArch64
`service` uses four encoding workers and baseline one-job admission/terminal
WriteBatches. No group commit, replacement kernel, or runtime test hooks.

## Build and run

All toolchain and test execution uses the pinned Linux broker:

```sh
python3 run.py './build.sh' 300
python3 run.py './tests/run.sh' 300
python3 run.py 'V1_SERVICE_PATH=/workspace/tmp/predecessor/service ./tests/run.sh' 300
python3 run.py './service DATADIR SOCKET_PATH'
```

The third command includes the actual predecessor upgrade lane. Its v1 executable
is preserved at `tmp/predecessor/service`; without V1_SERVICE_PATH that one test
is explicitly skipped. All other tests are self-contained within the supplied
infrastructure. The original source, tests, handoff and experiment record are also
