## Implementation and ownership

- `src/native.rs`: C-compatible v2 items use arena-relative uint64 offsets and
  sizes. A worker retains source bytes, arena, item/result arrays and bitmap
  until verification returns. Native bit i is checked against status == 0 for
  item i; all 64 bits are supported without shifting by 64. Wire results remain
  the specified per-item status/sizes/digests; there is no added bitmap field.
- `src/protocol.rs`: typed high/normal priority, default normal on submit and
  missing legacy pending fields. Invalid priorities are rejected. Priority is
  not in the payload digest; retry never changes admission metadata.
- `src/scheduler.rs`: two FIFO queues owned by the state thread. With both
  nonempty, dispatch high/high/high/normal cyclically. A single nonempty queue
  dispatches without advancing the cycle. Empty periods also preserve phase.
- `src/main.rs`: recovered jobs enter their priority queues in sequence order;
  durable queued cancellations do not enter the encoder. Newly accepted
  cancellations remove queued entries after their intent write succeeds, without
  consuming a dispatch turn. Four worker slots and admission-ordered terminal
  commitment are retained.

The state/storage owner remains the only database writer. Admission stores the
complete payload/index/accounting before acknowledgment. Cancellation writes
intent with sync/WAL before acknowledgment. Running cancellations await worker
return, keeping arenas alive. Completed out-of-order work stays charged until
its contiguous terminal commit. Receipts, pending/cancel removal, accounting and
checkpoint advance atomically; ID indexes remain retained. C write call_entry
is the terminal boundary, not the later barrier before the underlying write.

Recovery validates existing schema, checkpoint, indexes, payload digest and
accounting, without rebuilding or rewriting old receipts. V1 jobs are normal;
v2 priorities are retained. Unsupported versions and invalid stored priorities
fail explicitly. Storage and acknowledged-job arena failures retain the last
complete durable state and do not produce false acknowledgments/receipts.

