## Assumptions and evidence limits

Cycle starts at the first high turn on process startup; the contract specifies
no persistent scheduler-phase key. Cancelled waiting jobs are not dispatches and
consume no turns. Nonpersistent evaluate work shares the normal queue. Missing
legacy priority means normal; explicit null/unknown priority is invalid.
These resolve prose ambiguities without changing the prescribed schema.

The predecessor's reserved-field, framing, and retry-during-drain interpretations
remain: reject unknown reserved fields, exclude newline from the 40 MiB text
bound, retain existing/conflict responses for retries during drain. The bitmap
convention was checked against the supplied native adapter, including bit 63.

No evaluator, other workspace, repository source outside this workspace, network,
Bitcoin library, native sanitizer variant, whole-service race detector or fault
injection infrastructure was accessed. Tests demonstrate sampled process-crash
recovery and deterministic owner dispatch, not exhaustive interleavings or
power-loss behavior. Native allocation/storage-error paths were reviewed but
not fault-injected. No gate/freeze execution or performance qualification is
claimed. No optimization hypotheses or group commit were used.

